<DocsLayout title="First document">
  <p>Launch MarkRust. A previous session can be restored; use the File menu to start a new document or open a file or folder.</p>

  <h2>Create a new document</h2>
  <p>Press <kbd>⌘N</kbd> on macOS or <kbd>Ctrl+N</kbd> on Windows/Linux to create an untitled document. <kbd>⌘T</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+T</kbd> creates another tab.</p>
  <p>Save with <kbd>⌘S</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+S</kbd> to choose a path. MarkRust writes plain UTF-8 Markdown.</p>

  <h2>Open an existing file</h2>
  <p>Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> to open a single <code>.md</code> file, or <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> to open a folder as a workspace.</p>
  <p>Use <strong>File → Open Location</strong> (<kbd>⌘⇧L</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+L</kbd>) to paste a file or folder path directly.</p>

  <h2>Write Markdown</h2>
  <p>Type normally. WYSIWYG renders headings, lists, emphasis, links, and code fences. <strong>View → Show Markup Hints</strong> controls optional syntax hints; Source mode shows Markdown text.</p>

  <h2>Draft recovery and saving</h2>
  <p>Draft checkpoints are separate from the document file. Save explicitly writes the file; a tab’s dot indicates unsaved changes. Recovery can restore unsaved work on the next launch. Windows recovery privacy and locking still require native acceptance.</p>
